        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(cloud-workers): session placement, dispatch, and worker turn routing",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCloud workers (issue #104294) can run agent turns on ephemeral boxes since milestone 2, but nothing routes a *session* onto a worker: there is no durable record of where a session executes, no dispatch flow that moves one there, and no recovery when the gateway restarts mid-dispatch. This PR delivers milestone 3's core: the placement state machine, workspace sync + session attachment, one-shot worker turn execution, dispatch/turn routing, and the session-placement RPC surface with startup reconciliation.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPer docs/plan/cloud-workers.md milestone 3: sessions need a durable, crash-safe placement lifecycle (local → requested → provisioning → syncing → starting → active(worker) → draining → reconciling → local | reclaimed | failed) with atomic turn admission so exactly one owner runs a turn at any time, and per-run worker admission so a worker can only execute the run it was dispatched for.\n\n- Placement rows live in the shared state DB (Kysely, synchronous CAS write transactions); dispatch, failure handling, and startup recovery are separate bounded modules.\n- Workspace sync reuses the milestone-2 tunnel: git bundles for git workspaces, manifest mirror for plain dirs. This fixes a real bug in the WIP: the setup script and rsync targets disagreed on the remote root, so git-mode sync could never work; both transfers now target the returned absolute remote workspace dir. Also adds a local symlink-escape guard mirroring the remote manifest guard (macOS openrsync fails opaquely on escaping symlinks).\n- Worker admission is now bound to (sessionId, runId): `sessions.dispatch` launches a one-shot embedded turn from the descriptor, and the service rejects inference/turn requests for runs the worker was not admitted for.\n- `sessions.dispatch` (operator.admin) closes local turn admission, drains active work, syncs, and returns once placement reaches active worker ownership; startup reconciliation moves interrupted placements to a safe state.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible change yet: the RPC surface is present only when a cloud-worker profile is configured, and no UI/dispatch tool ships in this PR (target-bar UI and the agent dispatch tool follow). Foundation for dispatching sessions to throwaway cloud machines with live sidebar visibility.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/worker-environments` — 66 files, 783/783 pass\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/worker` — 4 files, 47/47 pass (includes the milestone-2 fault-injection gate updated for per-run admission)\n- tsgo lanes: core, core-test, test-root — all pass\n- `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs` — baseline matched, zero unexpected\n- plugin-sdk surface test 10/10; oxlint clean on touched trees; all prod files ≤500 LOC\n- Structured autoreview (Codex) on the branch diff before landing\n",
